ing, especially when attacking Japanese ground forces on the island. A total of 9,588 Airacobra aircraft were manufactured from 1940 to 1944, including many variants.","LocalizedString":"The Bell P-39 Airacobra was an American fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1941 and was used by the US air forces and their Allies during WWII. The aircraft saw combat in the Pacific, Mediterranean and on the Eastern Front. Some were used by the Cactus Air Force in the Battle of Guadalcanal and although it wasn’t on par with contemporary Japanese fighters it performed well in bombing runs and conducting strafing, especially when attacking Japanese ground forces on the island. A total of 9,588 Airacobra aircraft were manufactured from 1940 to 1944, including many variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Campaign2020","isReserved":true,"showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamageAddDamage"],"draftBaseWeight":0.8,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_p-39_l.t_p-39_l","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Bot","artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/P-39_AIRACOBRA.P-39_AIRACOBRA","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":278.0},"historyPhotoSource":"USAAF","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p39_airacobra_photo","SourceString":"Bell P-39Q Airacobra in flight, ca 1942.","LocalizedString":"Bell P-39Q Airacobra in flight, ca 1942."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_p39_airacobra_header","SourceString":"Fighter Aircraft","LocalizedString":"Fighter Aircraft"},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionAircraftM'","ObjectPath":"kar